{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"aerobic-exploitive-xraytetra","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`AGENTS.md:225` and `docs/exit-codes.md:183` still advertise `rebar review`, but `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:406`, `src/rebar/llm/operations.py:146`, and the release record establish that the route was removed.\n\n## Approach\n\nCorrect the two maintained pages directly to use the live review-plan/review-code guidance and their actual exit behavior. Keep ownership beside the command and governance documentation; do not add a new command-reference generator.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `AGENTS.md`\n- `docs/exit-codes.md`\n- existing CLI/documentation checks if they assert removed-command guidance\n\n## Testing\n\nRun a repository search for the retired invocation in maintained guidance and execute the existing help/exit-code documentation checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Maintained agent guidance no longer instructs users to invoke `rebar review`.\n- [ ] Exit-code guidance reflects the current review-plan/review-code commands and their real outcomes.\n- [ ] A targeted maintained-documentation search finds no obsolete review-command instruction outside historical records.\n- [ ] Existing CLI and documentation checks pass without expanding generation ownership.","id":"2dbf-07bf-452d-4543","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":2,"tags":["janitor","documentation","cli","rp22"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove obsolete review-command guidance from maintained CLI documentation"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788313775846218001,"uuid":"705d2f77-e7be-4223-a3bc-2a488b5cd2eb"}